# Line-ending and diff policy for shadowdark-extras.
#
# Why this file exists: several source files had been committed with CRLF (one
# of them mixed, 1787 of 2303 lines), which makes `git diff --check` report
# phantom "trailing whitespace" on any line touched inside a CR region and
# produces whole-file diffs when an editor rewrites the endings. core.autocrlf
# is a per-developer setting and cannot prevent that on its own -- a
# contributor with different settings can still commit CRLF blobs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Store text as LF in the repository. Working-tree endings are NOT forced here:
# they still follow each developer's core.autocrlf, so Windows checkouts keep
# CRLF locally exactly as before. Only what Git stores is normalized.
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Text formats (explicit, so the heuristic is never consulted)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mjs      text
*.js       text
*.json     text
*.json5    text
*.yml      text
*.yaml     text
*.css      text
*.hbs      text
*.html     text
*.md       text
*.txt      text
*.svg      text

# Shell scripts must be LF in the working tree too -- CRLF breaks the shebang
# and produces "bad interpreter" / "\r: command not found" at runtime.
*.sh       text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary assets - never normalize, never diff as text
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.webp     binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.ico      binary

*.mp3      binary
*.mp4      binary
*.webm     binary
*.ogg      binary
*.wav      binary

*.ttf      binary
*.otf      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.eot      binary

*.pdf      binary
*.zip      binary

# NOT listed as binary: *.rtf. RTF is plain ASCII markup and is already stored
# as LF here; marking it binary would stop normalization and let the CRLF from
# a Windows working tree back into the blob.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compendium artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Built packs are LevelDB and are normally generated by CI rather than
# committed, but if one ever lands in a branch it must not be treated as text:
# normalizing a .ldb or MANIFEST would corrupt the pack.
packs/**            binary
*.ldb               binary
**/MANIFEST-*       binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diff quality of life
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mjs      diff=javascript
*.js       diff=javascript
*.css      diff=css
*.html     diff=html
*.md       diff=markdown
